#. type: Title ###
#: ../src/cookbook/custom-hydrator-type-casters.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Null and invalid values"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/cookbook/custom-hydrator-type-casters.md
msgid "Here is what happens with a property declared as `?UserId` for different input values:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/cookbook/custom-hydrator-type-casters.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Input value                              | Handled by             | Property value                   |\n"
"|------------------------------------------|------------------------|----------------------------------|\n"
"| `'0192f2a4-7a4b-7c3e-9a1b-3f5c8d2e6a10'` | `UuidValueTypeCaster`  | `UserId` instance                |\n"
"| `null`                                   | `PhpNativeTypeCaster`  | `null`                           |\n"
"| `'not-a-uuid'`                           | none, all casters fail | default value, `null` in example |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/cookbook/custom-hydrator-type-casters.md
msgid "The last row is the important one: the hydrator doesn't report the malformed value.  With the `Required` rule, validation catches it with the \"cannot be blank\" error.  See the [request input](#request-input) and [form model](#form-model) examples.  But if the property is optional, an invalid UUID is silently turned into `null` and is indistinguishable from a missing value. If that's not acceptable, keep the raw value for validation: declare the property as `string`, validate its format, and convert it to the value object after validation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/cookbook/custom-hydrator-type-casters.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "When to use a type caster"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/cookbook/custom-hydrator-type-casters.md
msgid "A type caster fits well when the conversion:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/cookbook/custom-hydrator-type-casters.md
msgid "depends only on the value and the declared type."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/cookbook/custom-hydrator-type-casters.md
msgid "is the same everywhere in the application."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/cookbook/custom-hydrator-type-casters.md
msgid "doesn't need I/O, such as database queries or HTTP calls."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/cookbook/custom-hydrator-type-casters.md
msgid "Value objects for IDs, emails, and money amounts match all three. Keep the conversion in a dedicated mapper or a domain factory instead when it:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/cookbook/custom-hydrator-type-casters.md
msgid "needs a database lookup, for example, turning an ID into a loaded entity."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/cookbook/custom-hydrator-type-casters.md
msgid "depends on context, such as the current user."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/cookbook/custom-hydrator-type-casters.md
msgid "combines several input fields into one object."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/cookbook/custom-hydrator-type-casters.md
msgid "differs between use cases."
msgstr ""
